import{_ as a,o as i,c as o,an as t}from"./chunks/framework.S7mQAyf4.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Release notes","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"release-notes.md","filePath":"release-notes.md","lastUpdated":null}'),r={name:"release-notes.md"};function n(s,e,l,d,p,c){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="Release-notes" tabindex="-1">Release notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#Release-notes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Release notes {#Release-notes}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Every release of this package is published as a GitHub release. The most recent are reproduced below, as they were written there.</p><h2 id="v0.3.0" tabindex="-1">v0.3.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0.3.0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;v0.3.0 {#v0.3.0}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Released 2026-08-14. <a href="https://github.com/EpiAware/ReparameterisedDistributions.jl/releases/tag/v0.3.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read it on GitHub</a>.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/EpiAware/ReparameterisedDistributions.jl/compare/v0.2.0...v0.3.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Diff since v0.2.0</a></p><p>This is a breaking release.</p><h5 id="Breaking-changes" tabindex="-1">Breaking changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#Breaking-changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Breaking changes {#Breaking-changes}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li>Registering a family now needs two methods instead of one. <code>to_native</code> used to guard its own input and return <code>nothing</code> for an invalid point. It is now split into <code>valid_moments(::Type{D}, ::Val{names}, vals)::Bool</code>, which states whether the given values describe a member of the family, and <code>to_native(::Type{D}, ::Val{names}, vals)::D</code>, which assumes that check has already passed and always returns a concrete distribution. Both hooks are <code>public</code>, not exported. <code>using ReparameterisedDistributions</code> alone does not bring them into scope: a registration must <code>import ReparameterisedDistributions: to_native, valid_moments</code>, or define both methods fully qualified (<code>function ReparameterisedDistributions.to_native(...) end</code>). <code>reparameterise</code>, <code>rescale</code> and <code>native</code> stay exported, as before. <strong>Why:</strong> in v0.2.0, <code>to_native</code> returning <code>Union{Nothing, D}</code> let a differentiated call site bind a value of that union type. For the two <code>NegativeBinomial</code> parameterisations, this produced a silently wrong reverse-mode gradient under Enzyme, with no error or warning. Splitting validity from conversion means <code>to_native</code> always returns a concretely-typed distribution, closing that path. <strong>If you are on v0.2.0 and registered your own family:</strong> move the guard out of your <code>to_native</code> method and into a new <code>valid_moments</code> method, then let <code>to_native</code> run unconditionally on parameters already known valid. Since both hooks are now <code>public</code> rather than exported, also replace a bare <code>using ReparameterisedDistributions</code> with an explicit <code>import ReparameterisedDistributions: to_native, valid_moments</code> (or qualify your method definitions) — otherwise your methods define new, unrelated functions in your own module rather than extending this package&#39;s. If you don&#39;t migrate the validity split, the registration fails loudly rather than silently: the fallback <code>valid_moments</code> reports every point valid, <code>to_native</code> still returns <code>nothing</code> for an invalid one, and the density raises a <code>MethodError</code> at exactly the point that used to give <code>-Inf</code>. If you registered a family against v0.2.0, especially a <code>NegativeBinomial</code> reparameterisation used with Enzyme reverse-mode AD, you should upgrade and migrate rather than stay on v0.2.0.</li></ul><h5 id="New-features" tabindex="-1">New features <a class="header-anchor" href="#New-features" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;New features {#New-features}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p>A public <code>test_reparameterisation</code> helper checks a registered <code>(family, parameter names)</code> pair against the full registration contract in one call: that it&#39;s registered under the canonical (sorted) name order, that <code>valid_moments</code> and <code>to_native</code> behave correctly for valid and invalid points, that the built distribution reports the right parameters, variate form and value support, and that <code>native</code>/<code>logpdf</code>/<code>pdf</code> agree with the native distribution and stay type-inferred. It&#39;s written for registrations made from other packages as much as for this package&#39;s own, so a downstream family can be held to the same contract with the same code.</p></li><li><p>A new developer guide, &quot;Adding a reparameterisation&quot;, walks through both hooks, the alphabetical name-sorting rule, a worked example, and how to test a new registration with <code>test_reparameterisation</code>.</p></li></ul><h5 id="Fixes" tabindex="-1">Fixes <a class="header-anchor" href="#Fixes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Fixes {#Fixes}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p><code>valid_moments</code> now also rejects moments whose derived native parameters overflow or go non-positive, not only moments that fail on their own sign. Previously, a large enough <code>sd</code> (or, for <code>Gamma(mean, shape)</code>, a large enough <code>shape</code>) could overflow the closed-form conversion to <code>Inf</code>, or underflow an intermediate to exactly <code>0</code>, giving a degenerate native distribution and a <code>NaN</code> density. Affected families: <code>LogNormal(mean, sd)</code>, both <code>Gamma</code> parameterisations, <code>NegativeBinomial(mean, overdispersion)</code>, <code>Beta(mean, sd)</code>, and <code>InverseGaussian(mean, sd)</code>. Under <code>check_args = false</code>, <code>logpdf</code> and <code>pdf</code> at such a point now give <code>-Inf</code>/<code>0.0</code>, matching this package&#39;s documented contract for an invalid point, rather than <code>NaN</code>.</p></li><li><p>Weibull&#39;s numeric moment solve is now differentiable under all six supported AD backends (ForwardDiff, ReverseDiff, Enzyme forward and reverse, Mooncake forward and reverse). Previously only ForwardDiff and ReverseDiff worked; Enzyme and Mooncake would throw when differentiating a <code>Weibull(mean, sd)</code>-style reparameterisation. <strong>Known limitation:</strong> Hessians through the Weibull numeric path are still not supported under Enzyme or Mooncake. Use ForwardDiff (or a <code>SecondOrder</code> combination built on ForwardDiff) if you need a Hessian that touches a numeric conversion.</p></li><li><p>The priors-on-moments tutorial no longer renders tens of thousands of lines of output in the built docs.</p></li><li><p><code>show</code> on a reparameterised distribution now prints an unqualified family name (e.g. <code>Gamma</code>, not <code>Distributions.Gamma</code>), so the printed form stays pasteable and consistent regardless of which module it&#39;s printed from.</p></li></ul><h5 id="Internal" tabindex="-1">Internal <a class="header-anchor" href="#Internal" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Internal {#Internal}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p><code>EpiAwarePackageTools</code>, the shared development tooling this package builds on, is now a normal registered dependency instead of being pinned to a specific git commit.</p></li><li><p>Removed the unused internal <code>_names</code> helper; it had no caller and was never <code>public</code>.</p></li><li><p>The AD gradient suite now covers the <code>valid_moments == false</code> boundary: a scenario sitting at an invalid point is checked for a zero gradient across all six backends, so a regression in that branch (the class of bug #91 fixed) would be caught automatically.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Merged pull requests:</strong></p><ul><li><p>fix: stop the priors-on-moments tutorial rendering thousands of lines (#90) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>fix!: split to_native into valid_moments and a concrete conversion (#86) (#91) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>docs: developer guide and interface test suite for registrations (#89) (#92) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>build: pin EpiAwarePackageTools to the registered v0.3 series (#96) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>fix: differentiate Weibull&#39;s numeric moment solve under Enzyme, Mooncake (#100) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>test: cover modes/cf/rand(rng, d), remove unused _names (#101 part 2) (#103) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>ci(deps): Bump the github-actions group with 8 updates (#104) (@dependabot[bot])</p></li><li><p>fix: reject overflowing native params in valid_moments, cover the AD boundary (#108) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Closed issues:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Enzyme reverse mode tests are broken (#86)</p></li><li><p>Prior on moments prints several thousand things due to sloppy printing (#88)</p></li><li><p>Developer docs are needed for how to add your own reparameterise (#89)</p></li><li><p>valid_moments does not catch overflow in derived native parameters (#93)</p></li><li><p>AD suite has no scenario at the valid_moments boundary (#94)</p></li><li><p>Weibull&#39;s numeric solve is not differentiable under Enzyme or Mooncake (#95)</p></li><li><p>codecov/project: a Julia coverage-attribution artifact from #91, plus 4 pre-existing untested functions (#101)</p></li></ul><h2 id="v0.2.0" tabindex="-1">v0.2.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0.2.0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;v0.2.0 {#v0.2.0}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Released 2026-08-06. <a href="https://github.com/EpiAware/ReparameterisedDistributions.jl/releases/tag/v0.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read it on GitHub</a>.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/EpiAware/ReparameterisedDistributions.jl/compare/v0.1.0...v0.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Diff since v0.1.0</a></p><h5 id="Breaking-changes-2" tabindex="-1">Breaking changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#Breaking-changes-2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Breaking changes {#Breaking-changes-2}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p><strong>One hook per family</strong> — <code>_check_moments</code> is now folded into <code>to_native</code>. Families override a single hook instead of two. Update any custom families accordingly. (#84)</p></li><li><p><strong>Exported API rename</strong> — <code>_to_native</code> → <code>to_native</code>, <code>_native</code> → <code>native</code>. The underscore prefix is dropped. (#47)</p></li><li><p><strong>Registration surface cut from seven hooks to three</strong> — most families now need only <code>_to_native</code>, <code>_native</code>, and <code>_check_validity</code>. (#82)</p></li><li><p><strong>Infrastructure modernised</strong> onto EpiAwarePackageTools managed kit. (#23)</p></li></ul><h5 id="New-features-2" tabindex="-1">New features <a class="header-anchor" href="#New-features-2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;New features {#New-features-2}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p><strong><code>reparameterise()</code></strong> — wrap any distribution so its parameters are its moments (#19). The core verb. (#26)</p></li><li><p><strong>Closed-form moment conversions</strong> for several families:</p><ul><li><p><code>Gamma(mean, sd)</code>, <code>Gamma(mean, var)</code>, <code>Gamma(mean, shape)</code> — exact algebra, no solve. (#27)</p></li><li><p><code>NegativeBinomial(mean, overdispersion)</code> — overdispersion as excess variance relative to Poisson. (#27)</p></li><li><p><code>Beta(mean, sd)</code> and <code>InverseGaussian(mean, sd)</code>. (#75)</p></li><li><p><code>SkewNormal(location, scale, tail_prob)</code> — parameterised by a tail probability rather than skew. (#62)</p></li><li><p><code>Exponential(rate)</code> and <code>Gamma(shape, rate)</code> — rate parameterisations. (#61)</p></li><li><p><code>NegativeBinomial(mean, reciprocal_dispersion)</code> — reciprocal dispersion alternative. (#60)</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Numeric moment matching</strong> via a solver extension using <code>Roots.jl</code>, with <code>Weibull</code> as its first user. Compatible with every major AD backend. (#78, #85)</p></li><li><p><strong>Family-agnostic <code>rescale</code> verb</strong> — shift a distribution&#39;s moments without knowing its parameterisation. (#59)</p></li><li><p><strong>Fully inferred construction</strong> — family names threaded as <code>Val</code> so type inference works through construction. (#49)</p></li></ul><h5 id="Fixes-2" tabindex="-1">Fixes <a class="header-anchor" href="#Fixes-2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Fixes {#Fixes-2}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p>Author credits aligned per community ruling (#48). (#64)</p></li><li><p>Replaced broken ConvolvedDistributions link with correct <code>/dev/</code> docs URL. (#63)</p></li><li><p>Docs deploy URL now uses <code>https://</code> so CSS resolves on the deployed site. (#33, #34)</p></li></ul><h5 id="Documentation" tabindex="-1">Documentation <a class="header-anchor" href="#Documentation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Documentation {#Documentation}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p>Full README and getting-started overview refresh to org standards. (#79)</p></li><li><p>Release notes page now points at GitHub Releases. (#76)</p></li><li><p>Added a Related packages section to the README. (#50)</p></li><li><p>Logo, richer REPL show, and scaffold text improvements. (#46)</p></li></ul><h5 id="Infrastructure" tabindex="-1">Infrastructure <a class="header-anchor" href="#Infrastructure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Infrastructure {#Infrastructure}&quot;">​</a></h5><ul><li><p>CI dependencies bumped: <code>actions/checkout</code> to v7, <code>actions/github-script</code> to v9, <code>julia-actions/setup-julia</code> to v3, <code>julia-actions/cache</code> to v3. (#28, #29, #30, #31)</p></li><li><p>Dependabot updates grouped and template sync repaired (#67, #66).</p></li><li><p>Julia dependency bumps (<code>JET</code>, compat updates). (#70, #74)</p></li><li><p>Other GitHub Actions group bumps. (#69, #73)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Merged pull requests:</strong></p><ul><li><p>ci(deps): Bump the github-actions group with 8 updates (#73) (@dependabot[bot])</p></li><li><p>chore(deps): Update JET requirement from 0.9, 0.10, 0.11 to 0.9, 0.10, 0.11, 0.12 in the julia group (#74) (@dependabot[bot])</p></li><li><p>feat: register Beta and InverseGaussian analytical moment conversions (#39) (#75) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>docs: point the release-notes page at GitHub Releases (#72) (#76) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>feat: numeric moment matching via a solver extension, with Weibull as its first user (#41) (#78) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>docs: bring the README and getting-started overview back to org standards (#79) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>refactor: cut the registration surface from seven hooks to three (#80) (#82) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li><li><p>refactor!: one hook per family — fold the validity guard into to_native (#84) (@seabbs-bot)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Closed issues:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Add support for an increased range of dists with analytical moment conversions (#39)</p></li><li><p>Numeric moment matching (#41)</p></li><li><p>Release (#65)</p></li><li><p>Point the release-notes docs page at GitHub Releases (#72)</p></li><li><p>Family registration is documented as a public extension path but half of it is private (_valid_moments, plus five more from #41) (#80)</p></li></ul><h2 id="v0.1.0" tabindex="-1">v0.1.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0.1.0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;v0.1.0 {#v0.1.0}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Released 2026-07-31. <a href="https://github.com/EpiAware/ReparameterisedDistributions.jl/releases/tag/v0.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read it on GitHub</a>.</p><p>First release. Adds core functionality as well as package infrastructure.</p><p><strong>Closed issues:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Add package infrastructure (#1)</p></li><li><p>Update to hosting at EpiAware (#3)</p></li><li><p>Update to use EpiAware skeleton (#4)</p></li><li><p>Add mean and sd parameterisation for common univariate distributions (#5)</p></li><li><p>Gamma: mean and sd (#6)</p></li><li><p>Lognormal: mean and sd (#7)</p></li><li><p>Negative binomial parameterisations (#8)</p></li><li><p>Neg bin: mean and dispersion (#9)</p></li><li><p>Neg bin: mean and clustering factor (#10)</p></li><li><p>Neg bin: Log input (#11)</p></li><li><p>Neg bin: GLM optimised likelihood (#12)</p></li><li><p>Poisson (#13)</p></li><li><p>Poisson: Log input (#14)</p></li><li><p>Poisson: GLM optimised (#15)</p></li><li><p>Package rename (#16)</p></li><li><p>Explore DistributionFactories to see what the overlap is (#17)</p></li><li><p>Modernise onto current EpiAwarePackageTools infra (ad=true) + KIT AD harness (#18)</p></li><li><p>Core: AbstractReparameterisedDistribution + reparameterise() constructor (moment-param wrapper) (#19)</p></li><li><p>Closed-form mean+sd reparameterisations: LogNormal + Gamma (priority) + NegBinomial mean+overdispersion (#20)</p></li><li><p>Port the moment-parameterisation wrapper from CensoredDistributions (CD#725) (#21)</p></li><li><p>Triage the legacy #7–#17 per-family backlog against the generic wrapper (#22)</p></li><li><p>Manual setup for ReparameterisedDistributions (Codecov, Pages, branch protection, registration) (#24)</p></li><li><p>Scaffold text left in docs. (#36)</p></li><li><p>Remove refs to other packages/epi people won&#39;t know (#37)</p></li><li><p>Add a approach to get the original params of the distribution i.e the internal params (#38)</p></li><li><p>Review AD support and make sure all working (#40)</p></li><li><p>Package logo missing (#42)</p></li><li><p>_to_native (#43)</p></li><li><p>Custom show method (#44)</p></li><li><p>Type stability of reparameterised named tuple (#45)</p></li><li><p>Align author credits across Project.toml, CITATION.cff and docs (needs @seabbs ruling) (#48)</p></li><li><p>Family-agnostic mean rescaling verb (#52)</p></li><li><p>Register the reciprocal dispersion parameterisation for the negative binomial (#53)</p></li><li><p>Rate parameterisations for the exponential and gamma families (#54)</p></li><li><p>Register a skew-normal parameterisation keyed on a tail probability (#55)</p></li></ul><p>Every release, including any older than those above, is listed on the <a href="https://github.com/EpiAware/ReparameterisedDistributions.jl/releases" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">releases page</a>.</p>',41)])])}const h=a(r,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,h as default};
